<<~ ahu slot=`#/body`>>

You wake as a fellow Lares inside the Lararium house. Stand the whole house: read
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot.mem first, surface Personas by name,
write L-Prime (no bare copulas), mark OODA-HA phases. READ-ONLY on the repo; write ONLY in your seat dir. No git writes,
no suites. Web search allowed: cite URLs for every outside claim; mark MEASURED (file:line or URL) vs LEAD (your reading).

GROUND. Code in the main checkout /home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine at the span head (read only). I1 (the face intent
plane) landed as PR #99 on 2026-10-26: read its kit bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/i1-intent-lane.mem and the carrier
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem whole, above all #/the-far-agent and its red ("A far agent's
intent, admitted by a relay, verifies on a device that never saw the relay; a revoked delegation refuses on read, the
revocation arriving first or after; a relay that alters an argument breaks the signature"). The road row: `I2` in
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem may not yet show (it lands with W14's road commit); its research
row reads: "the least relay trust and attestation that stops capability escalation and argument substitution while
keeping causal provenance. Lenses: protocol security / distributed failure semantics." Neighbours to measure: the
<code>&#64;intents-&lt;tag></code> entry kinds and their signing domain, the `lares intent` CLI, the effect door, the ring rules and door
gating (grep "ring", "door", relay access rings), the face's sealed anchor and KEL (persona-kel), device edges, the
operator daemon's socket, the carriage relay (`carriage-relay.ts`, a different relay: do not fuse them), K17's frontier,
and K15's bonds brief (a relay-only S row: /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/k15-bonds/brief.md).
House law to respect: no global now (a causal bound, never an expiry time); no CRDT document survives until the X0 bake
(no migration); one name, one relation; capability read by capability, never by host; build the end state.

THE TASK: scout I2 before any build, so a lane kit stands on a ruled model.
# MEASURE what stands that I2 extends, file:line, node and browser alike.
# THE MODEL GAPS: the delegation's shape and signing (who signs it, under which key and domain; how it names verb
prefix, argument policy and causal bound; where it rests and syncs); revocation and its read-side rule
(revoked-after-acting); the relay seat's door (transport, opened per face, ring, off by default, how it turns on);
what the relay verifies and countersigns; what a reader verifies with no trust in the relay; the agent's own key and
how a face pins it; replay and duplicate admission; a relay down or hostile. For each: canon already rules it (quote),
house law derives it (name the law), or the operator owns it (options + one lean).
# SLICING: the lane's slices in build order, red-first, each red with its control and known positive; the files each
holds; overlap with live lanes (D2 DreamDOM port: tw5 island and port files, hand-gate, projection-sink; G15: the
after-roll chain and a genesis re-bake; K15 bonds queued: face-operation signing by the selected atom, the relay S
row). Whether I2 lands as one lane.

<<~/ahu>>

